From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] widescreen auto-UI: ignore stray front world primitives for
 overlays

A screen-space overlay counts as being in front of the world when its OT
rank is above the world's front bound. That bound was the front-most world
primitive, so one polygon crossing the near plane and clamped to the last
OT rank put the bound in front of the overlay and un-squashed it for that
frame. The bound now skips up to 1% of the world's primitives (at least
one) at the front.

Fixes Action Man: Operation Extreme's bow scope flashing back to the
stretched, broken-apart mask for a frame when looking down at the floor:
one floor polygon at rank 1023 sat in front of the mask (1016..1022).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/src/gpu.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/runtime/src/gpu.c b/runtime/src/gpu.c
index 9a0d3da..5cf6b53 100644
--- a/runtime/src/gpu.c
+++ b/runtime/src/gpu.c
@@ -7026,9 +7026,20 @@ void gpu_ws_prepass_linked_list(uint32_t start_addr) {
      * kinds: squashing only the axis-aligned pieces tore holes in the mask
      * and split the bow's wings. */
     if (provenance && ws_ui_world_total) {
-        uint32_t world_max = 0;
-        for (uint32_t r = 0; r < WS_UI_WORLD_RANKS; r++)
-            if (ws_ui_world_rank_count[r]) world_max = r;
+        /* The front of the world, ignoring a stray front-most primitive or
+         * two: a polygon crossing the near plane can be clamped to the last
+         * OT rank, in front of the overlay. Up to 1% of the world (at least
+         * one primitive) may lie in front of the bound. Action Man's bow scope
+         * looking down at the floor put one floor polygon at rank 1023, in
+         * front of the mask (1016..1022), and the whole scope un-squashed for
+         * that frame. */
+        uint32_t world_max = 0, stray = ws_ui_world_total / 100u + 1u;
+        for (uint32_t r = WS_UI_WORLD_RANKS; r-- > 0;) {
+            const uint32_t c = ws_ui_world_rank_count[r];
+            if (!c) continue;
+            if (c > stray) { world_max = r; break; }
+            stray -= c;
+        }
         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < ws_ui_prepass_count; i++) {
             if (ws_ui_prepass[i].enclosed_only &&
                 ws_ui_prepass[i].ot_rank > world_max) {
